---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import ImageFigure from '../components/ImageFigure.astro';
import gt3 from '../assets/screenshots/gallery_488_gt3_laguna_seca.webp';
import { LINKS } from '../lib/site';
import { reportUrl } from '../data/roadmap';
import {
  CARS,
  CAR_SYSTEMS,
  LOADED_TRACKS,
  LOOSE_OBJECTS,
  REFUSED_CARS,
  REFUSED_TRACKS,
  REFUSED_TRACK_REASON,
  TRACKS,
  TRACK_LIMITS,
} from '../data/compatibility';

const description = `Which Assetto Corsa cars and tracks load in rustyAC: ${CARS.loaded} of ${CARS.installed} installed cars and all ${TRACKS.loaded} drivable track layouts. What is refused, and why.`;

const TOC = [
  { id: 'cars', label: 'Cars' },
  { id: 'tracks', label: 'Tracks' },
  { id: 'csp', label: 'Custom Shaders Patch' },
  { id: 'check', label: 'Check your own install' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Compatibility"
  intro="On the install it is tested on, every car and track that plain Assetto Corsa can load, loads in rustyAC. Content made only for Custom Shaders Patch is refused."
  description={description}
  toc={TOC}
>
  <ul class="tally">
    <li class="card">
      <span class="tally__n mono">{CARS.loaded}<span class="tally__of"> / {CARS.installed}</span></span>
      <span class="muted">installed cars load</span>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <span class="tally__n mono">{TRACKS.loaded}<span class="tally__of"> / {TRACKS.entries}</span></span>
      <span class="muted">track layouts load and drive</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <!-- rustyAC docs/port/audio.md, "Cars": the 123 are the cars installed on the PC the reports were written on -->
  <p>
    These counts are for one Assetto Corsa install, the one rustyAC is tested on: the base game, some of its DLC and
    a few mods. They are not a count of everything ever made for the game.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cars">Cars</h2>
  <!-- docs/port/suspensions.md, sections 1 and 4 -->
  <p>
    <strong>{CARS.loaded} of the {CARS.installed} installed cars load.</strong> The {CARS.refused} that are refused
    need Custom Shaders Patch, and plain Assetto Corsa cannot run them either.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Refused car</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          REFUSED_CARS.map((car) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono">{car.folder}</td>
              <td>{car.reason}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The reports name cars by their folder under <code>content\cars</code>, so that is what is listed here.</p>

  <h3>What a car can have</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        {
          CAR_SYSTEMS.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{row.what}</th>
              <td>{row.detail}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <!-- packaging/HOW_TO_RUN.txt, section 1; docs/port/suspensions.md, section 5 -->
  <p>
    <strong>Mods work when plain Assetto Corsa can load them.</strong> A car with a plain <code>data</code> folder (an
    unpacked mod, the SDK's cars) is read from that; <code>--car</code> also takes the path of a car's folder.
  </p>

  <ImageFigure
    src={gt3}
    alt="A Ferrari 488 GT3 on track at Laguna Seca, drawn by rustyAC"
    caption="The Ferrari 488 GT3 at Laguna Seca."
    sizes="(min-width: 1184px) 856px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 328px), (min-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 48px), calc(100vw - 32px)"
  />

  <h2 id="tracks">Tracks</h2>
  <!-- docs/port/tracks.md, section 1 -->
  <p>
    <strong>All {TRACKS.loaded} drivable layouts load, drive and time laps.</strong> The install has {TRACKS.folders} track
    folders with {TRACKS.entries} entries in the track menu; the other {TRACKS.refused} are refused with a reason.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Point-to-point tracks work</strong> (the Trento-Bondone hill climb, the Nordschleife tourist layout): the
      clock starts at the start gate and the run is listed when you pass the finish gate.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Loose cones work.</strong> {LOOSE_OBJECTS.tracks} of the tracks have loose objects ({LOOSE_OBJECTS.objects} in
      all: cones and marker boards). They sit still until the car's body hits them, then fly, tumble and come to
      rest.
    </li>
    <li>Laps and sectors are timed from the track's own timing lines, and a lap is spoiled by the game's own rule.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The {TRACKS.loaded} layouts that load</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Track folder</th><th>Layouts</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          LOADED_TRACKS.map((track) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono">{track.folder}</td>
              <td>
                {track.layouts.length > 0 ? <span class="mono">{track.layouts.join(', ')}</span> : <span class="muted">one layout</span>}
                {track.note && <span class="muted"> ({track.note})</span>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>The {TRACKS.refused} that are refused</h3>
  <!-- docs/port/tracks.md, section 6 -->
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Track / layout</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          REFUSED_TRACKS.map((track) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono">{track.entry}</td>
              <td>{REFUSED_TRACK_REASON[track.kind]}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>What is not there yet</h3>
  <ul>
    {TRACK_LIMITS.map((limit) => <li>{limit}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="csp">Custom Shaders Patch</h2>
  <!-- docs/port/awd_ers.md, section 6 ("CSP is closed source"); docs/port/tracks.md, sections 6 and 8 -->
  <p>
    Custom Shaders Patch (CSP) is a closed-source add-on that changes Assetto Corsa itself, and some cars and tracks
    are made only for it. rustyAC is a port of plain Assetto Corsa and does not implement CSP.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Refused</strong> means rustyAC stops with a message that names the file and the reason, instead of
    loading something it would get wrong. Each refused car and track above is either not installed or made only for CSP, and plain Assetto Corsa cannot
    load it either. Nothing is decrypted.
  </p>
  <!-- rustyAC README.md; docs/port/grip_investigation.md -->
  <p>
    One more thing to know: if CSP is switched on in your own Assetto Corsa, the same car will not handle the same
    there as in rustyAC. CSP changes the physics, even for a standard car. rustyAC matches the game without it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="check">Check your own install</h2>
  <!-- packaging/HOW_TO_RUN.txt, section 2 -->
  <p>Your install is not the one above. To see what yours has:</p>
  <pre><code>rustyac.exe --list-tracks</code></pre>
  <p>
    It lists every track and layout of your game, and which ones cannot be driven and why. A car that cannot load
    says so when you start it with <code>--car</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The details are in the reports: <a href={reportUrl('suspensions.md')} rel="noopener">cars and suspensions</a>,
    <a href={reportUrl('tracks.md')} rel="noopener">every track</a>. Found something that should load and does not?
    <a href={`${LINKS.github}/issues`} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a>.
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .tally {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .tally li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
  }

  .tally__n {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .tally__of {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.5em;
  }

  th[scope='row'] {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    background: none;
  }
</style>
